{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3819","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3819","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3819\",\"parent_revision\":\"3b8970e99d4e0995897b2f84f7f0f9e2c7f088c548f8b0b0c42984bc545925b2\",\"root_revision\":\"3b8970e99d4e0995897b2f84f7f0f9e2c7f088c548f8b0b0c42984bc545925b2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe repository evaluation path does not execute the behavioral skill inventory end to end. Direct `run_eval.py` usage is description-oriented, so this session required a separate OpenCode runner. That runner also exposed three contract gaps: provider setup did not initially load the existing Portkey configuration correctly, process exit 0 did not prove that a model produced a final answer, and prose grading could demand model fields that belong to structural validation.\\n\\nBuild one maintained behavioral runner that:\\n\\n- executes isolated skill and baseline arms from `evals/evals.json`;\\n- supports the repository Portkey/OpenCode configuration through environment indirection;\\n- requires a real final answer/stop signal in addition to process exit 0;\\n- validates declared fixture isolation, hashes, credential leakage, and target-skill absence in baselines;\\n- uses production model/schema validation for structural expectations and prose grading only for behavioral expectations;\\n- persists complete transcripts and a reproducible grading report.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Verification observations from #3784\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"45591ecc07428cd9db539394a7ca6c1a020c06c32742cd3e16898f0de746c92f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCEP1w\"}"}